  "title": "osf review: multi-agent PR review pipeline",
  "summary": "Adds a full pull-request review subsystem to osf. A new `osf review` command family (run / reduce / work-item) selects review lenses from a shipped catalogue of 20, drives coding agents (codex, claude, opencode, omp, dsh) headless in a clean copy of the change, validates each answer against a JSON Schema, verifies every quoted finding against the real file, and reduces the answers to a pass/fail/could-not-run verdict. A new GitHub Actions workflow runs one reviewer per job with only its own provider key, then a final job mints a verifier app token and posts the review. Supporting changes: an agent registry with hook wiring and read-only modes, a builder-family detector that sits out reviewers from the family that wrote the change, secret redaction of prompts and findings, and suppression ownership so a marker naming another checker's rule is no longer reported unused.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
